      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (from [[write-journal]]) describes a safety mechanism in the guarded write path of the agent runtime. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function:** Before any file is overwritten, the system records the file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content if it existed, or a record that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n\n**Rollback on failure:** If an agent run fails (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order:\n- Restores previous content for files that existed\n- Deletes newly created files\n\n**All-or-nothing semantics:** This gives each agent run atomic write behavior without needing a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of one run.\n\n**Query agent specifics:** The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback path since it has no write tool at all, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5558,
      "output_tokens": 231
    }
